      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Current implementation in fcrepo-1026 branch, and proposed documentation at ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA36/Validation"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA36/Validation",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Outstanding issue:  HTTP status codes - current foxml validation error results in a 500.  A 400 code (perhaps 422, but this is a webdav extension so could be regarded as non-standard from a purist REST standpoint, though people do use it) would be more appropriate.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Would this constitute a breaking change for the REST API?  One could argue the case that the current 500 codes for validation errors are in fact a bug, as it's not a server error.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
