  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Currently validation is somewhat configurable:  A custom validation module could be written and configured in fedora.fcfg.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This isn't that flexible as it means that if the existing validation was also to be carried out, then that would need to be called by the custom validator.  A better design pattern might be something like the management Decorator pattern we already used.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We also might consider allowing validators to operate on the digital object, rather than a file or inputstream - it may be more convenient for the validator to access the object itself rather than FOXML.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We perhaps also might distinguish between different types of validation, eg validation of the FOXML vs validation of the object - the FOXML is a serialisation of the object, it is not the object itself. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Existing validation on doCommit() (DefaultDOManager) only happens in debug - but the validator is invoked on ingest separately.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The existing validation could be refactored so that the XML validation and schematron validation become decorator implementations.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We should also consider relationships validation (which is carried out by the ValidationUtility, and not included in the DOValidatorImpl).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Perhaps the REST validate endpoint could also be extended (and configurable) to validate using the above as well as the current ECM validation.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
